0 29 663 [
[(The previous example showed one way you can programmatically add and alter)]
[(scalars. This one shows how to add a structure to the "put" menu so that you)]
[(can easily add one to new windows. \050If you've just made a new structure this)]
[(is the easiest way to create its first scalar.\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 28 594 [
[(It's also often convenient to specify initial values when new scalars are)]
[(created. You can do this by adding the initial value for a field after its)]
[(declaration, as in the arguments "float z 20", etc, in the [struct] for this)]
[(example. Pd can tell that it's an initialization because it's a number and not)]
[(a symbol. Either way, if there's a following argument that one should be a)]
[(symbol giving the next type \050so far, this has always been "float"\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
