0 30 490 [
[(The struct04 window catches most editing actions and uses a [trigger] object)]
[(to peel off the pointer in the message coming from [struct]. The messages have)]
[(additional arguments that depend on the particular action. The patch prints)]
[(them out so you can see them all.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 31 423 [
[(It is sometimes useful to catch editing moves such as run-mode clicks and to)]
[(display some or all of the field values so that you can see and/or modify them)]
[(numerically. In this example it's done right in the "struct04" window.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 83 220 [
[(You can also crweate scalars by sending a 'scalar' message to)]
[(a window. The arguments of this message is template name and)]
[(its field values in the order that the "struct" object lists)]
[(them. This is intended as an internal message used to save and)]
[(recall patches - use at your own risk.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 33 370 [
[(The [struct] here doesn't include rectangles to show hot points \050as the first)]
[(example did\051 but you can still drag the top vertices of the triangles up and)]
[(down \050changing z\051 and the right ones left and right \050changing w\051. These)]
[(changes are reflected in the struct04 subpatch.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
